  "callouts": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Lingua Franca BT paper (ICSE 2024): a Reader before a Writer on channel x cannot take a same-tick cable. The compiler inserts Pre, gated by start, because BT ticks are not a fixed after delay.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 24,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 220
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "1 \u00b7 Select Pre. Store this tick's x; emit it when start fires again. Output x is ordinary this-tick data. z\u207b\u00b9 is the Block, not a backward cable.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1144,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 200,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "b-pre",
        "anchor": "left",
        "dy": -50
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2",
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "C's back edge is Temporal \u2192 Delayed: dotted cable + z\u207b\u00b9 pill. Same Pre semantics on the edge. Never a solid reverse data cable.",
      "x": 2140,
      "y": 1804,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 180
    },
    {
      "id": "pass",
      "kind": "pass",
      "text": "PASS WHEN the legend's four cables are distinct, Pre has no solid reverse data cable, C's back edge is dotted with a z\u207b\u00b9 pill, and D's dashed / mut cables are clearly not delay.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 2304,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 220
    }
  ]
